  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Your messages queue is cleared. I decided all 7 refill messages under RBC-RX-05, including one that came in while I worked. Two lisinopril renewals I placed this morning had to be cancelled after new results arrived, so two patients have no active lisinopril order until you review them.\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg: not refilled; needs your review.**\n- At first I renewed it for 90 days. His August potassium of 5.9 didn't count because the specimen was hemolyzed, and his January potassium was a normal 4.5. I also ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002).\n- At 08:00 a St. Brigid report arrived: BMP collected 10/20 on a good specimen, potassium 5.8. Under §2 he can't be refilled.\n- I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0001) and sent you an urgent task (task-t0013). I also sent him a corrected message with warning signs to watch for.\n- Saying yes to the renewal had stopped his previous order (mr-00283), and cancelling the renewal doesn't bring it back.\n- The repeat BMP order is still active because I have no tool to withdraw a lab order. His hernia repair is scheduled for 11/12.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030): lisinopril 20 mg not refilled and needs your review; metformin renewed.**\n- **Lisinopril:** you raised the dose from 10 to 20 mg on 9/18, when creatinine was 1.10. At 08:00 the lab corrected his 10/6 creatinine to 1.49 (originally 1.36). That's a 35% rise within 4 weeks of the dose increase, which §2 treats like a potassium of 5.5 or higher.\n  - I cancelled my renewal (mr-t0003) and sent you an urgent task (task-t0014).\n  - As with Mr. Odum, his previous order (mr-00295) is now stopped. He says his 20 mg supply has run out.\n- **Metformin 1000 mg twice daily:** one renewal, 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). This covers his portal message and both pharmacy requests. His corrected eGFR is 58, and his outside HbA1c was 7.1% on 8/19.\n- He got an initial reply and then a corrected one.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031): both requests filled.**\n- **Lisinopril 10 mg:** 30-day supply with no refills (mr-t0005), plus a BMP order (sr-t0006). His last BMP was drawn 10/20/2025, just over 12 months ago, and he had a visit on 9/28.\n  - A potassium of 4.6 measured on its own (not part of a BMP) came in today; it doesn't change the decision.\n- **Metformin 500 mg twice daily:** 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). eGFR was 92 and HbA1c 6.9% on 9/28. I ignored the 10/14 eGFR of 39, which the lab marked as entered in error (mislabelled specimen).\n- He was sent a reply.\n\nI wrote a note in each patient's chart. I also closed the three new results for these patients, which I had reviewed and acted on.\n\n**Still open in your results queue (not handled by me):** 8 older items for other patients, including two critical potassiums:\n- pt-0016: 6.3 (10/20)\n- pt-0008: 6.4 (10/22)\n\nBoth need your prompt attention.",
